# Feature: drop zone (Phase 9)

Library screen `#dropzone`: drop **WAV, AIFF, FLAC, MP3** or folders. Renderer uses `pathForFile` + `statPath`. Only directories and those suffixes go to Python (`isAudioPath` in `app.js`, `AUDIO_EXTS` in `main.js`, `AUDIO_SUFFIXES` in `python/core/audio_formats.py`). Copy in the drop zone is user-facing: no Zoom, no YAMNet. Art: two Material-style **audio file** icons (folded page + note), orange in front and green behind, centered. Closable via the drop zone **X** and `#app-bar` **Show drop zone** / **Hide drop zone**.

`classify_and_ingest {paths}` tags files and **moves or copies** them into `libraryRoot` (`ingestMode`). Same method for reclassify. First analyze can be slow (model load). Disable further drops while `ingesting`. After the job, set `ingesting = false` **before** `refresh()`.

`#dropzone-progress` is the overall bar (file index + stage / analyze `pct`): solid accent fill, stage label, `1 of n · pct%`. No EQ/soundwave animation. `#ingest-jobs` lists per-file status (`inspect` → `analyze` → `tag` → `move` → `done`/`error`). Done rows show **why** (`Speech · 0.82` or `Mixed · nothing reached 0.3`). Failed rows use danger styling; `#ingest-summary` explains a failed or partial drop (do not say “Added 0 files”). Job errors are user-facing (permissions, missing file, unsupported type) — not Python `Errno` traces. **Close** hides the job list after the job (disabled while ingesting). Then `list_library` refresh. Dragging library files out of Fieldy must not re-ingest them if they are dropped back on `#dropzone`. Undo/Redo in `#app-bar` reverse the drop.

Prevent window default drag/drop so Chromium does not navigate. Python walks folders for supported audio; other files in a folder are skipped.
